# Implementation review

After implementation and focused tests, perform **one** independent review.
Do not run review councils, repeated closure audits, or an audit of the audit.

## Focus areas

- correctness
- business-use-case alignment
- architecture boundaries
- database and tenant safety
- security
- migration safety
- test quality
- accidental scope expansion

## Severity

Report **BLOCKER**, **HIGH** and **MEDIUM** only.

- **BLOCKER** and **HIGH** must be fixed before commit.
- **MEDIUM** may be fixed or recorded in `HANDOFF.md`.

## Independence

Prefer a read-only reviewer or fresh pass that did not author the change.
The implementing agent may incorporate fixes; do not invent a second process layer.

## Out of scope for this review

- production legal/regulatory closure
- approval-queue completeness
- owner decision packets
- canonical migration admission
- full enterprise governance suite (unless epic/milestone/production-readiness)

## Exit

When BLOCKER/HIGH are cleared and focused verification passes: update
`HANDOFF.md`, then create **one coherent commit** (only when the user asks).
